I am walking home.
I have two cloth bags in my hands.
The bags are very heavy.
I want some rest now.
There is a brown street dog on the road.
I see that dog.
The dog comes near me.
I look at the dog carefully.
It sniffs my bag.
There are fresh vegetables in the bag.
It sniffs the tomatoes and onions.
I have a dog at my home in Mexico.
Her name is Lola.
I like dogs very much.
But I want these vegetables.
I slowly pass the dog.
The dog looks at me.
It stays right there.
I walk forward.
I safely reach my flat.
